Fix WarmCachePanel auto-polling. Minimal patch: in the existing useEffect after fetchStatus(), if status.running is true, also start the polling interval; OR add a second useEffect that watches status?.running and starts/stops pollRef accordingly. Example:

    useEffect(() => {
      if (status?.running && !pollRef.current) {
        pollRef.current = setInterval(fetchStatus, 1500);
      }
      if (!status?.running && pollRef.current) {
        clearInterval(pollRef.current); pollRef.current = null;
      }
    }, [status?.running]);

This way the admin sees live progress whether they clicked the button OR landed on the tab while a startup-triggered warm-up is already running — exactly what the spec describes ('clicking still shows the live progress').
